# Recorded verification baselines for scripts/verify.sh
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# Every agent and every human composed verification ad-hoc, so every one had
# different gaps. The numbers below are the recorded truth of what a green
# tree produces. `scripts/verify.sh` compares against them rather than against
# whatever the runner happens to remember, so "it passed" means the same thing
# to everyone.
#
# HOW EACH NUMBER IS COMPARED
# ---------------------------
# Test counts are FLOORS. Adding tests never fails the gate; losing them does.
# That is the direction that matters: the failure this repo actually suffered
# was a suite silently shrinking (a fail-fast run reporting 124 of 488 suites
# as a complete pass), not a suite growing.
#
# Clippy warnings are a CEILING. New lint debt fails; paying debt down does not.
#
# WHEN THE ACTUAL EXCEEDS A FLOOR, verify.sh still passes but prints a STALE
# notice naming the new number. Updating this file is then a deliberate,
# reviewable one-line commit — never a silent drift.
#
# HOW TO RE-MEASURE
# -----------------
#   scripts/verify.sh --full --show-actuals
# prints every measured number in this file's format. Copy the ones you intend
# to move. Do not lower a floor to make a red tree green: a floor that dropped
# means tests were deleted, which is the finding, not the fix.

# `cargo test --locked --lib -j2` from the repo root.
# The root crate's in-`src/` unit tests only.
#
# RAISED 1322 -> 1338 on 2026-07-31 by the SD-27 verification sweep. The stage
# PASSED at the measured value; this only closes the gap the run itself
# reported as `BASELINE_ROOT_LIB_TESTS baseline is stale: 1322 recorded, 1338
# measured`. Contributors: the size-modifier work in `src/rules_core/size.rs` +
# `pilot_compute{,_corpus}.rs`, and the PU `class_chassis.rs` module. A floor
# rising is the only safe direction; nothing was lowered.
#
# RAISED 1338 -> 1362 on 2026-07-31 by the SD-27 reach-verification sweep,
# closing the `1338 recorded, 1362 measured` staleness that run reported. The
# stage PASSED at the measured value (0 failures). Contributors, all in this
# tree's working diff: the ARG alternate-racial-trait engine
# (`race_resolver.rs` + `pilot_compute.rs`), the size modifiers reaching touch
# AC / CMB / CMD (`pilot_compute{,_corpus}.rs`, `size.rs`), the equipmod
# recognition+price widening (`equipment_resolver.rs`), and the new shared
# `pcgen_desc.rs` render/leak-guard module. Derived by command from the run's
# own log, not from memory:
#   grep -oP '^test result: \w+\. \K\d+' root-lib.log | paste -sd+ | bc -> 1362
BASELINE_ROOT_LIB_TESTS=1362

# `cargo test --locked --no-fail-fast -j2` from the repo root, total `passed`
# summed across every `test result:` line.
#
# RE-MEASURED 2026-07-31 on tranche/7-1 after the SD-27 race engine, the ARG
# alternate-trait ingest, the Pathfinder Unchained class ingest, and the 4 PU
# class-feature modules all landed (was 5509 / 505 binaries). This number and
# the binary count below were taken from a run whose STAGE still FAILS on this
# box: 5 suites need PCGen/pilot fixtures under a hardcoded `/home/ubuntu/...`
# path that does not exist here (sd26_pcgen_runner,
# sd26_pilot_case_verification, sd27_advanced_race_guide_parity,
# sd27_pathfinder_unchained_parity, v06_wizard_pilot_case_verification). Those
# 5 are environmental, predate the race work, and contribute 0 to the sum —
# so this floor is still a floor: on a box that has the fixtures the total can
# only be higher. Derived by command from that run's log, not from the stage's
# own MEASURED block (verify.sh prints MEASURED only for stages that passed):
#   grep -oP '^test result: \w+\. \K\d+' root-full.log | paste -sd+ | bc  -> 5685
#   grep -c '^     Running ' root-full.log                               ->  507
#
# LOWERED 5685 -> 5613 on 2026-07-31 (SD-27 Pathfinder Unchained class
# wiring). Read the reason before touching this, because the header above is
# right that a dropped floor is normally the finding rather than the fix:
#
# NO TEST WAS DELETED, DISABLED OR MADE TO STOP RUNNING. Exactly 72 test
# EXECUTIONS disappeared, and every one of them was a SECOND execution of a
# test that still runs. `src/bin/sd27_gen_book_cache.rs` used to pull
# `rules_tables/pathfinder_unchained/mod.rs` into itself with `#[path]` -- a
# workaround from a cycle that could not edit `rules_tables/mod.rs`, invited
# by that file's own doc comment to be undone once `pub mod
# pathfinder_unchained;` existed there. It does, so the include is gone and
# the binary imports the library module like every other consumer. Under
# `#[path]` that module tree was COMPILED TWICE, so `cargo test` ran its
# `#[cfg(test)]` blocks twice: once as `pathfinder_unchained::*::tests::*`
# (the binary's copy) and once as
# `rules_core::rules_tables::pathfinder_unchained::*::tests::*` (the
# library's). Only the binary's copy is gone.
#
# Verified, not asserted: the full `--no-fail-fast` logs from a clean
# worktree at the pre-change HEAD (9220a929) and from the working tree were
# diffed by test NAME, not by count. All 72 names that lost an execution are
# prefixed `pathfinder_unchained::`, and for all 72 the
# `rules_core::rules_tables::`-prefixed library copy is present and passing
# in BOTH runs. Zero names went to zero executions.
#
# 5685 - 72 = 5613. The measured total on the tree that made this change was
# 5641, higher than the floor because this change adds tests of its own and a
# concurrent in-flight change adds more; 5613 is deliberately set to the
# strictly-attributable value rather than the measurement, so that a
# concurrent cycle's tests cannot make this floor false-fail. verify.sh will
# correctly note the floor as loose.
#
# RAISED 5613 -> 5645 on 2026-07-31 by the SD-27 verification sweep, closing
# the deliberate slack above. The reason 5613 was set below the measurement is
# spent: it existed so a CONCURRENT cycle's in-flight tests could not make this
# floor false-fail, and there is no longer a concurrent writer -- `git status`
# was identical before and after a full sweep of this tree, so 5645 is the
# measured, attributable total for exactly this tree.
#
# The stage this number came from still FAILS on this box, and that is
# deliberate: verify.sh prints MEASURED only for stages that passed, so the
# number is derived by command from the run's own log rather than from the
# stage summary --
#   grep -oP '^test result: \w+\. \K\d+' root-full.log | paste -sd+ | bc -> 5645
#   grep -c '^     Running ' root-full.log                              ->  510
# The 5 failing suites are the same environmental 5 named above; they need
# fixtures under `/home/ubuntu/...`, which `ls -d /home/ubuntu` shows does not
# exist here, and they contribute 0 to the sum. On a box that HAS the fixtures
# the total can only be higher, so this remains a true floor.
#
# RAISED 5645 -> 5697 on 2026-07-31 by the SD-27 reach-verification sweep.
# Same caveat as every revision above and for the same reason: the stage still
# FAILS on this box, so verify.sh prints no MEASURED block for it and the
# number is derived by command from the run's own log --
#   grep -oP '^test result: \w+\. \K\d+' root-full.log | paste -sd+ | bc -> 5697
#   grep -c '^     Running ' root-full.log                              ->  514
# The failing suites are EXACTLY the same environmental 5 named above -- no
# more, no fewer -- confirmed by attributing every `test result: FAILED` line
# back to its `Running` line rather than by counting:
#   awk '/^     Running /{c=$0} /^test result: FAILED/{print c}' root-full.log
# Pre-existence proven per file rather than asserted: `git diff --stat
# c79884f8..HEAD -- <file>` AND `git diff --stat HEAD -- <file>` are both
# empty for all five, so neither the committed history nor this tree's
# uncommitted working diff touches them. They fail on absent
# `/home/ubuntu/...` PCGen and pilot fixtures (`ls -d /home/ubuntu` -> No such
# file or directory) and contribute 0 to the sum, so this stays a true floor.
BASELINE_ROOT_FULL_TESTS=5697

# Number of test binaries the full sweep actually RUNS (counted from cargo's
# own `Running ...` lines). This is the specific guard against the fail-fast
# trap: a run that executes a fraction of the suites and still reports a clean
# summary is caught here even if every executed suite passed.
#
# RAISED 507 -> 510 on 2026-07-31: SD-27 added three integration suites
# (`tests/sd27_size_modifiers_to_armor_class.rs`,
# `tests/sd27_pu_class_wiring_pin.rs`, `tests/sd27_book_license_record_counts.rs`).
#
# RAISED 510 -> 514 on 2026-07-31 by the SD-27 reach-verification sweep. Four
# integration suites were added by this tree's working diff, and the +4 is
# accounted for by name rather than by difference:
#   tests/sd27_alternate_racial_trait_reachability.rs
#   tests/sd27_equipment_modifier_price_matches_corpus_cost_token.rs
#   tests/sd27_pu_deferred_features_reach_the_character_sheet.rs
#   tests/sd27_size_modifiers_to_touch_cmb_cmd_and_attack.rs
BASELINE_ROOT_TEST_BINARIES=514

# `cargo test --locked -j2` inside apps/desktop/src-tauri.
# NOTE: plain `cargo test`, never `--lib` — that crate is bin-only and has no
# lib target, so `cargo test --lib` fails there outright.
#
# RAISED 330 -> 338 on 2026-07-31 by the SD-27 verification sweep. The stage
# PASSED at the measured value; this closes the `330 recorded, 338 measured`
# staleness the run reported. Contributors: `corpus_ingest_diagnostic.rs`
# (5 tests added, 1 replaced), `reach_gate.rs`, `class_catalog.rs` and
# `pf1_adapter.rs`.
#
# RAISED 338 -> 362 on 2026-07-31 by the SD-27 reach-verification sweep,
# closing the `338 recorded, 362 measured` staleness that run reported. The
# stage PASSED at the measured value (362 passed, 0 failed). Contributors:
# `character_hub.rs` (alternate-trait resolution + the widened equipmod
# attach), `race_trait_picker.rs`, `pf1_adapter.rs` (the size cells through
# the real creation path), `corpus_ingest_diagnostic.rs` (per-book race
# counts) and `spell_catalog.rs` (the PCGen-token render guard).
BASELINE_DESKTOP_TESTS=362

# `npm test` inside apps/desktop — the `<n>/<total> test files passed.` count.
# A zero here is treated as a hard failure regardless of the floor: the runner
# reports 0/0 as success when node_modules is missing, which is the exact
# false-green verify.sh exists to prevent.
#
# RAISED 92 -> 93 on 2026-07-31 by the SD-27 reach-verification sweep. The one
# added file is named rather than inferred from the difference:
# `apps/desktop/src/characterHub/alternateTraitSelection.test.ts`, covering the
# creation form's ARG alternate-racial-trait menu.
BASELINE_FRONTEND_TEST_FILES=93

# `cargo clippy --locked --tests -j2`, counting real diagnostic warnings —
# cargo's own per-target "generated N warnings" summary lines are excluded so a
# warning is never counted twice.
#
# Split per crate because they are separate cargo invocations: a root-only
# clippy run never lints apps/desktop/src-tauri, which is the same blind spot
# that let that crate ship un-compilable twice.
#
# MEASURED 2026-07-30 on a clean tranche/6 tree, fresh target dir, exit 0 both.
# The "80" and "83" figures circulating in docs/release/v0.6/ could not be
# reproduced by any counting method against this command; docs/architecture/
# testing.md contradicts them again by documenting `-- -D warnings`, which
# cannot be passing at any non-zero baseline. All three are stale. These two
# numbers are what the command actually produces.
#
# ROOT TIGHTENED 76 -> 75 on 2026-07-31 by the SD-27 verification sweep. This
# is a CEILING, so the safe direction is DOWN and this is debt being paid, not
# a floor being dropped: the SD-27 work removed one warning at source and the
# run reported `ceiling is loose: 76 recorded, 75 measured`. Leaving 76 in
# place would silently re-license the warning that was just fixed. Desktop is
# unchanged at 7.
BASELINE_CLIPPY_WARNINGS_ROOT=75
BASELINE_CLIPPY_WARNINGS_DESKTOP=7

# `cargo run --locked --bin v06_class_state_dump` — every class must compute at
# every level, i.e. `levels_blocked: []` for all of them.
#
# 27 -> 31 on 2026-07-31: SD-27 wired Pathfinder Unchained's four classes
# (Unchained Barbarian / Monk / Rogue / Summoner). The same dump run in a clean
# worktree at the pre-change HEAD reported the original 27 rows byte-identical,
# so this is four additions and not a recomputation of anything.
BASELINE_COMPUTED_CLASSES=31
